      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Source, lighting model and expected result",
      "description": "Original synthetic aligned intensity fixtures by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors (MIT). No external/customer images or equipment I/O. Input pixels are aligned by construction; Pixel grid does not perform registration. truth.json records lighting formulas, injected defects and channel coefficients. Compare raw and adjusted residuals on the same valid inspection population. Image remains original; Adjusted preserves source depth/encoding; contours highlight defects. This is empirical appearance compensation, not physical radiometric calibration. Large defects or texture changes can be learned as illumination; choose known-good fit regions and an appropriate local window. EXPECT FAIL: an 8x8 corner fit region cannot support local correction across the entire image. Coverage fails; unsupported pixels retain original samples and have zero adjusted residual, so always consume Valid mask.",
